WEBVTT

00:07:57.941 --> 00:08:00.210
And if, let's say,
you get out of your car,

00:08:00.243 --> 00:08:02.545
and instead of doing
jumping jacks, you just say,

00:08:02.579 --> 00:08:06.349
"OK, I'm going to relax now.
Relax now. You, relax!"

00:08:06.383 --> 00:08:07.784
Not effective, right?

00:08:07.817 --> 00:08:12.055
You've relaxed, but you haven't changed
your body's physiological state

00:08:12.088 --> 00:08:14.024
into one of safety.

00:08:14.057 --> 00:08:15.358
CSB: Totally.

00:08:15.392 --> 00:08:17.360
And our first question from the audience.

00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:19.462
OK, from Facebook, someone asks,

00:08:19.496 --> 00:08:22.332
"How do you know whether
what you're experiencing is burnout

00:08:22.365 --> 00:08:24.000
or something else?”

00:08:24.034 --> 00:08:26.736
EN: Yeah, ask a medical
professional for sure.

00:08:27.170 --> 00:08:34.177
And there's a lot of overlap between
burnout and lots of other experiences,